config DEMO_BLINK_MS
	int "LED toggle period in milliseconds"
	default 1000
	help
	  Every vendor release blinks at the default, once a second. The
	  attacker's builds set 250, and so does the factory command left in
	  the v1.x releases.

config DEMO_GOT_YOU
	string "Attacker banner"
	help
	  Set only in the attacker builds (attacker/*.conf). When not empty the
	  application prints "Got you! <this>" after its banner, so the
	  audience sees attacker code running.

config DEMO_FACTORY_UNLOCK
	bool "Leftover factory unlock command"
	default y
	help
	  The known hole in the v1.x releases: MCUmgr command 1 of the fuse group clears
	  the simulated debug lock and speeds up the blink. The v2.x releases and the attacker builds turn it off.
	  Replaying a genuine, signed v1.1.0 brings it back unless MCUboot
	  refuses downgrades.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
